[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3056501029","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107006#issuecomment-3056501029","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107006","id":3056501029,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62LoEl","user":{"login":"Rudolph-B","id":52322745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzIyNzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52322745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B","html_url":"https://github.com/Rudolph-B","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T09:17:48Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T09:17:48Z","body":"I agree subtracting 1 from the size argument would be the preferred solution.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3056501029/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058293965","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107006#issuecomment-3058293965","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107006","id":3058293965,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62SdzN","user":{"login":"jamie-pate","id":682658,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MjY1OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/682658?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate","html_url":"https://github.com/jamie-pate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T17:17:21Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T17:26:10Z","body":"`.reserve()` Increases the capacity... according to https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/vector/reserve \r\nthere is no `hopes` to increase the capacity..\r\n\r\n`LocalVector` seems to have the same guarantees.\r\n\r\n> relying on `reserve` for padding makes me uneasy\r\n\r\nNormally I would `assert(write_ptr == occ_inst->xformed_vertices.ptr() && occ_inst->xformed_vertices.get_capacity() >=  occ_inst->xformed_vertices.size() + 3);` when I get this kind of paranoia :D","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058293965/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058317375","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107006#issuecomment-3058317375","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107006","id":3058317375,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62Sjg_","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T17:26:04Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T17:26:04Z","body":"`xformed_vertices` is a `LocalVector`, not `std::vector`. Admittedly, it also creates the necessary capacity, at least as long as there's RAM left.\n\nStill, it makes me uneasy to rely on capacity semantics. For example, the objects will never be constructed or destructed. This is not important for SIMD padding, but it is important in other contexts. I think the size based method is just generally more robust.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058317375/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058319595","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107006#issuecomment-3058319595","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107006","id":3058319595,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62SkDr","user":{"login":"jamie-pate","id":682658,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MjY1OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/682658?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate","html_url":"https://github.com/jamie-pate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T17:26:59Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T17:30:08Z","body":"This is literally the reason for having `reserve()` and `capacity()` in addition to `resize()` and `size()`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058319595/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058348551","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107006#issuecomment-3058348551","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107006","id":3058348551,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62SrIH","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T17:38:55Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T17:40:41Z","body":"No, it is not. `reserve` exists mainly to speed up adding elements by avoiding repeated reallocations. At least, thats what i see it being used for most of the time.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3058348551/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3060766249","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107006#issuecomment-3060766249","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107006","id":3060766249,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62b5Yp","user":{"login":"Rudolph-B","id":52322745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzIyNzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52322745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B","html_url":"https://github.com/Rudolph-B","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-11T06:17:16Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T06:17:16Z","body":"For me, the minus-one method is preferred because it makes it clear that the padding was added specifically for that `rtcSetSharedGeometryBuffer()` function call. Currently, if you read the function, you wouldn’t expect it to behave any differently from other buffer-sharing functions. Admittedly, this could also be clarified with a comment.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3060766249/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3062955089","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107006#issuecomment-3062955089","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107006","id":3062955089,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62kPxR","user":{"login":"jamie-pate","id":682658,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MjY1OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/682658?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate","html_url":"https://github.com/jamie-pate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-11T16:33:12Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T16:56:05Z","body":"I like the reserve method because then the LocalVector behaves 'normally' in all cases, but also fulfills the requirements of `rtcSetSharedGeometryBuffer()`. The constraints are managed by the data structure which reduces the complexity of the function.\r\n\r\nTo do the padding aproach I'd want to introduce a new constant for the padding amount, and subtract it every single time you access the size of the LocalVector. Looking closer at the code, the size would need to be adjusted in multiple places. (which happened automatically with the `reserve()` approach, but I had to dig through the code and find them all to implement the padding approach. I still feel like reserve() is 'automatically correct' is the better approach.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3062955089/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5651303558","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107006#issuecomment-5651303558","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107006","id":5651303558,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUNgMhg","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-13T05:08:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T05:08:05Z","body":"The last message I heard from @jamie-pate was on July 5th, 2026. He has been silent for the last two months.\r\n\r\n@jamie-pate Farewell.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5651303558/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]